Z||000000||Galen||05-01-2001||12:40 PM||||I know that didn't sound too good hehe.. but anyways.  What do you hav in your hole above your radiater? what type of screen?mesh?what?<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||05-01-2001||01:06 PM||||don't stick anything in it.. it'll get lopped off! <P><BR>LMAO!!..<P>it's stainless steel mesh off an intake screen from an Amiad centrifugal Irrigation Filter. I used this cause the Aluminum i used on the Gold SE i had would oxidize. and have sooo much in the paint on this car i didn't wanna skimp on anything obvious..       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> the mesh is about $20 a foot. the screen i used ont he Gold SE was just aluminum gutter guard that was $1.88 for 3"x7.5" strip you'll only need on piece and you;ll have plenty left over... hope that helps...<P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstintake1.JPG">      <P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">      <BR>      <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  <A HREF="http://www.epdyno.com" TARGET=_blank>www.epdyno.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.enthuzacar.com" TARGET=_blank>www.enthuzacar.com</A> <BR>   <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Galen||05-01-2001||01:14 PM||||cool.. seeing as how I have very lil money.. I'll go for the cheap stuff.. hehe..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> how did you attach it? just screws in the underside of the trunk or?<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||05-01-2001||02:06 PM||||the Gold car i used clear epoxy.. this one i used fiber-glas resin. the epoxy was a better choice.. and it's cheaper. the resin even though the surface was scuffed up and preped properly the stainless doesn't flex and is cracking the inside of the hood. the aluminum does flex and might not cause this condition. <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
